AI Job Application Agent
An AI-powered automation platform that helps users discover jobs, analyze job descriptions, generate ATS-friendly resumes, apply automatically or semi-automatically, and track applications.
Overview
Automates repetitive job application workflows.
Uses AI, browser automation, and resume intelligence.
Supports scalable and modular architecture.
Main Goals
Automatically discover jobs.
Match jobs with user skills.
Generate customized resumes.
Track interview and application progress.
High-Level Architecture
Frontend Dashboard (Next.js)
API Gateway (Node.js + Express)
Job Scraper Service
AI Matching Engine
Resume Engine
Application Automation Engine
Tracking & Analytics Dashboard
Core Modules
Authentication Module
User Profile Module
Resume Parsing Module
Job Scraper Engine
AI Matching Engine
Resume Customization Engine
Application Automation Engine
Notification System
Analytics Dashboard
Automation Workflow
User uploads resume
AI extracts skills
Job scraper collects jobs
AI calculates match score
Resume is customized
Browser agent applies automatically
Dashboard tracks results
Recommended Technology Stack
Frontend: Next.js, Tailwind CSS
Backend: Node.js, Express.js, TypeScript
Automation: Playwright, browser-use
AI: Ollama, OpenAI, Claude
Database: MongoDB / PostgreSQL
Queue: Redis + BullMQ
Security Considerations
Encrypt user resumes and credentials.
Use JWT and refresh tokens.
Avoid aggressive automation.
Implement rate limiting and retry logic.
Folder Structure
apps/frontend
apps/backend
services/scraper-service
services/ai-service
services/apply-service
shared/utils
docs
docker
MVP Roadmap
Phase 1: Resume upload + job scraping
Phase 2: Resume customization
Phase 3: Semi-automatic applications
Phase 4: AI multi-agent workflows
Conclusion
The platform acts as a personal AI career assistant.
It improves ATS optimization and automates repetitive workflows.
A semi-automatic workflow is recommended for safer production usage.